<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="e9f27dd">&lt;p&gt;
    The change impact analysis queries change program members and business stakeholders to identify types of changes
    necessary for adoption of the solution.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    New solutions typically affect the dimensions of organization structure, roles, skills, process, systems, management
    interactions, infrastructure, environment, and safety. The assessment helps to determine the number of impacted people,
    specific impacts on individuals and business units, degree of those impacts and change dimension they affect.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The information gathered will inform planning for enabling activities: business engagement including communications,
    business readiness including organization design and training, business adoption including post implementation support.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The impact analysis information is shared with business sponsors, stakeholders, and change management leaders to
    understand actions they need to take to prepare people for change and help transition the organization to adopt the new
    business solution.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
